From: strix-rdma contributors <devnull@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] thunderbolt: add nonblocking native path ownership for service teardown

The native service worker must not wait for tb->lock while domain removal
holds that lock and waits for service work. Add opt-in software-CM-only
try operations and retire the exact admitted tuples before synchronous
XDomain removal. Existing path APIs retain their blocking behavior.

Up to two exact tuples are admitted per XDomain: the control ring pair and
the zero-copy data ring pair. EAGAIN never transfers ownership. ENODEV from
native disable is release-published only after core cleanup; DMA ring
stop/join remains the client's responsibility. Domain stop retires native
paths before generic tunnels. With CONFIG_INFINIBAND_STRIX_NHI disabled the
new fields and APIs are compiled out. Three behavior-preserving pieces
remain: the __tb_approve_xdomain_paths/tb_approve_xdomain_paths lock split,
a tb_cm_ops forward declaration and a call to the empty
tb_xdomain_remove_native_paths stub.

---
